const e={id:"exp-routing-params",title:{en:"Routing, Route Parameters & Query Strings",hi:"Routing, Route Params (:id) & Query Strings (?search=)"},difficulty:"Beginner",readTime:9,sections:[{type:"concept",heading:{en:"1. What is Routing & express.Router()?",hi:"1. Routing Aur express.Router() Kya Hai?"},body:{en:'**Routing** refers to how an application responds to a client request to a particular endpoint, defined by a specific URI (or path) and an HTTP request method (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE).\n\nIn a tiny demo app, writing all routes directly on `app.get()` in one file works. But in a real enterprise application with hundreds of endpoints, putting everything in `server.js` creates an unmaintainable monolithic disaster!\n\n### Modular Routing with `express.Router()`\nExpress provides `express.Router()`, which acts like a "mini-application" capable only of performing middleware and routing functions.\nYou create dedicated router files:\n- `src/routes/userRoutes.js` mounted at `/api/users`\n- `src/routes/productRoutes.js` mounted at `/api/products`\n- `src/routes/orderRoutes.js` mounted at `/api/orders`\n\n### Route Parameters vs Query Strings:\n- **Route Parameters (`req.params`)**: Part of the URL path used to identify a **specific resource** (`GET /api/users/:userId`).\n- **Query Strings (`req.query`)**: Optional key-value pairs appended after a `?` used for **filtering, searching, sorting, and pagination** (`GET /api/products?category=laptop&sort=asc&page=2`).',hi:"**Routing** ka matlab hota hai ki jab koi client kisi specific URL aur HTTP method (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE) par request kare, toh server use kaise respond karega.\n\nChote project mein sab kuch `server.js` mein likhna chal jata hai, par production apps mein jahan 100+ endpoints hote hain, wahan sab kuch ek file mein likhna bohot gandi practice hai.\n\n### `express.Router()` Se Modular Routing\nExpress humein `express.Router()` deta hai jo ek mini-app ki tarah kaam karta hai. Hum har feature ki alag route file banate hain:\n- `userRoutes.js` -> `/api/users` ke liye\n- `productRoutes.js` -> `/api/products` ke liye\n- `orderRoutes.js` -> `/api/orders` ke liye\n\n### Route Params vs Query Strings:\n- **Route Parameters (`req.params`)**: URL path ka hissa hote hain jo kisi **specific item ko identify** karte hain (jaise `/users/:id`).\n- **Query Strings (`req.query`)**: URL ke aage `?` laga kar bheje jaate hain aur data ko **filter, search, sort ya paginate** karne ke kaam aate hain (jaise `/products?category=phone&limit=10`)."}},{type:"concept",heading:{en:"2. The Route Ordering Rule & URL String Pitfall",hi:"2. Route Ka Sequence Aur String Type Ki Problem"},body:{en:'Two fundamental rules govern Express route matching:\n\n### Rule 1: First Match Wins (Route Sequence Matters!)\nExpress evaluates routes strictly in the order they are defined in code.\nIf you define a dynamic parameter route first:\n```javascript\napp.get(\'/users/:id\', ...);\napp.get(\'/users/profile\', ...); // NEVER REACHED!\n```\nWhen a request arrives for `/users/profile`, Express matches `:id` to the string `"profile"`! The specific route is shadowed and will never execute.\n> **Rule: Always place specific, static routes BEFORE generic dynamic parameter routes!**\n\n### Rule 2: Everything in `req.params` and `req.query` is a STRING!\nEven if the client visits `/users/101?limit=10`:\n- `req.params.id` is the string `"101"`, NOT the number `101`.\n- `req.query.limit` is the string `"10"`, NOT the number `10`.\nIf you pass them directly to math operations or strict equality checks (`=== 101`), comparisons will fail unless you cast them with `parseInt()` or `Number()`.',hi:'Express routing ke do sunahre niyam:\n\n### Niyam 1: Jo Pehle Aayega Wo Pehle Chalega (Order Matters)\nExpress routes ko upar se neeche sequence mein match karta hai.\nAgar aapne dynamic param wala route upar likh diya:\n```javascript\napp.get(\'/users/:id\', ...);\napp.get(\'/users/profile\', ...); // YEH KABHI NAHI CHALEGA!\n```\nJab koi `/users/profile` par aayega, toh Express `:id` ko `"profile"` samajh kar pehle wale route ko chala dega!\n> **Niyam: Specific static routes ko hamesha dynamic (:id) routes ke UPAR likhein!**\n\n### Niyam 2: Params Aur Queries Hamesha STRING Hoti Hain!\nChahe URL `/users/99?page=2` ho:\n- `req.params.id` string `"99"` hoga, number `99` nahi.\n- `req.query.page` string `"2"` hoga.\nAgar aap direct `if (req.params.id === 99)` check karenge toh comparison fail ho jayega! Hamesha `Number(req.params.id)` se convert karein.'}},{type:"analogy",heading:{en:"Real-Life Analogy: The Multi-Specialty Hospital Navigation",hi:"Real-Life Analogy: Bada Hospital Aur Room Numbers"},body:{en:'Imagine navigating **AIIMS Hospital in New Delhi**:\n\n- **The Main Reception (Root App)**: You enter the gate (`app.use(\'/cardiology\', cardiologyRouter)`).\n- **The Department Wing (The Modular Router)**: You are guided to the Cardiology Wing.\n- **The Room Number (Route Parameter - `:roomNo`)**:\n  - The board says: *"Go to Room #304"* (`/rooms/:roomNo`).\n  - `req.params.roomNo` = `"304"`. It identifies the exact physical location of that patient.\n- **The Doctor Search Filter (Query Parameter - `?status=available&experience=10`)**:\n  - At the inquiry desk, you ask: *"Show me doctors who are currently available with 10+ years experience"*.\n  - You are not identifying a room; you are filtering and querying the list of doctors!',hi:`Sochiye aap kisi bade **Hospital** mein jaate hain:

- **Main Gate (Root App)**: Gate par likha hai *"Heart Department ke liye Wing B mein jayein"* (\`app.use('/heart', heartRouter)\`).
- **Department Wing (Modular Router)**: Heart department ki apni alag building hai.
- **Room Number (Route Param - \`:roomNo\`)**:
  - Doctor ne kaha: *"Room #204 mein admit ho jao"* (\`/rooms/:roomNo\`).
  - Yeh specific patient ka exact address hai (\`req.params.roomNo\`).
- **Inquiry Filter (Query String - \`?available=true&fee=500\`)**:
  - Reception par aap puchte ho: *"Wo doctors dikhao jo abhi baithe hon aur fees 500 se kam ho"*.
  - Yeh kisi specific room ka naam nahi hai, yeh list ko filter karne ke criteria hain!`}},{type:"syntax",heading:{en:"4. Syntax: express.Router, req.params & req.query",hi:"4. Syntax: express.Router, req.params Aur req.query"},body:{en:`\`\`\`javascript
import express from 'express';

const router = express.Router();

// 1. Route Parameter (:id)
router.get('/:productId', (req, res) => {
  const { productId } = req.params;
  res.json({ id: productId });
});

// 2. Query String Extraction (?search=keyboard&sort=desc)
router.get('/', (req, res) => {
  const { search = '', sort = 'asc', page = 1, limit = 10 } = req.query;
  res.json({ search, sort, page: Number(page), limit: Number(limit) });
});

// 3. Route Chaining with router.route()
router.route('/orders')
  .get((req, res) => res.json({ action: "List orders" }))
  .post((req, res) => res.json({ action: "Create order" }));

export default router;
\`\`\``,hi:`\`\`\`javascript
import express from 'express';

const router = express.Router();

// 1. Route Param (:id)
router.get('/:id', (req, res) => {
  const id = req.params.id;
  res.json({ userId: id });
});

// 2. Query Parameters (?category=laptops&limit=5)
router.get('/', (req, res) => {
  const category = req.query.category;
  const limit = Number(req.query.limit) || 10;
  res.json({ category, limit });
});

// 3. Clean Route Chaining
router.route('/items')
  .get((req, res) => res.json([]))
  .post((req, res) => res.json({ saved: true }));

export default router;
\`\`\``}},{type:"example",heading:{en:"5. Practical Examples: Modular Product Router, Nested Params & Chaining",hi:"5. Practical Examples: Modular Router, Nested Params aur Query Filtering"},body:{en:"### Example 1: Modular Product Router with Query Filtering\nDemonstrates how to search, filter by price range, and paginate data with `req.query`.",hi:`### Example 1: Products Filtering Router (Search, Sort, Pagination)
Query strings se data ko filter aur sort karne ka production code.`},code:{language:"javascript",filename:"productRoutes.js",snippet:`// Example 1: Modular Product Router (src/routes/productRoutes.js)
import express from "express";

const router = express.Router();

const mockProducts = [
  { id: 1, name: "Mechanical Keyboard", category: "electronics", price: 3500 },
  { id: 2, name: "Wireless Gaming Mouse", category: "electronics", price: 1800 },
  { id: 3, name: "Ergonomic Desk Chair", category: "furniture", price: 9500 },
  { id: 4, name: "USB-C Fast Charger", category: "electronics", price: 1200 },
  { id: 5, name: "Wooden Laptop Stand", category: "furniture", price: 1500 }
];

// GET /api/products?category=electronics&maxPrice=3000&sort=asc
router.get("/", (req, res) => {
  let results = [...mockProducts];
  const { category, maxPrice, sort } = req.query;

  // 1. Filter by category
  if (category) {
    results = results.filter(p => p.category.toLowerCase() === category.toLowerCase());
  }

  // 2. Filter by maximum price (cast string to number!)
  if (maxPrice) {
    const numMaxPrice = parseFloat(maxPrice);
    results = results.filter(p => p.price <= numMaxPrice);
  }

  // 3. Sort by price
  if (sort === "asc") {
    results.sort((a, b) => a.price - b.price);
  } else if (sort === "desc") {
    results.sort((a, b) => b.price - a.price);
  }

  res.status(200).json({
    count: results.length,
    filtersApplied: { category, maxPrice, sort },
    products: results
  });
});

// GET /api/products/:id
router.get("/:id", (req, res) => {
  const productId = parseInt(req.params.id, 10);
  const product = mockProducts.find(p => p.id === productId);

  if (!product) {
    return res.status(404).json({ error: "Product not found" });
  }

  res.status(200).json(product);
});

export default router;`}},{type:"example",heading:{en:"Example 2: Nested Route Parameters (Users -> Orders -> Items)",hi:"Example 2: Nested Route Parameters (/users/:userId/orders/:orderId)"},body:{en:`### Example 2: Multi-Level Relational Routing
Extracting multiple parameters from deeply nested RESTful URLs.`,hi:`### Example 2: Multi-Level Relational Routing
URL se multiple dynamic IDs extract karna.`},code:{language:"javascript",filename:"nestedRouting.js",snippet:`// Example 2: Deeply Nested Route Parameters
import express from "express";

const app = express();

// GET /api/users/:userId/orders/:orderId/items/:itemId
app.get("/api/users/:userId/orders/:orderId/items/:itemId", (req, res) => {
  // Destructure multiple route parameters cleanly
  const { userId, orderId, itemId } = req.params;

  console.log("Extracted IDs:", { userId, orderId, itemId });

  res.status(200).json({
    message: "Retrieved nested line item successfully",
    hierarchy: {
      user: \`USR_\${userId}\`,
      order: \`ORD_\${orderId}\`,
      item: \`ITEM_\${itemId}\`
    }
  });
});

app.listen(5002, () => console.log("Nested router listening on port 5002"));`}},{type:"example",heading:{en:"Example 3: Clean Endpoint Chaining with router.route()",hi:"Example 3: router.route() Se Clean Endpoint Chaining"},body:{en:"### Example 3: Eliminating Duplicate Path Declarations\nUsing `router.route('/path')` to chain GET, POST, PUT, and DELETE handlers together cleanly without repeating the URI path.",hi:`### Example 3: router.route() Chaining Pattern
Same path ke liye GET, POST, DELETE handlers ko bina path repeat kiye clean chain karna.`},code:{language:"javascript",filename:"chainedRoutes.js",snippet:`// Example 3: Chaining HTTP Methods on the Same Route
import express from "express";

const router = express.Router();

// Chain GET and POST on '/api/articles'
router.route("/articles")
  .get((req, res) => {
    res.json({ message: "List of all published articles" });
  })
  .post((req, res) => {
    res.status(201).json({ message: "New article created" });
  });

// Chain GET, PUT, and DELETE on '/api/articles/:id'
router.route("/articles/:id")
  .get((req, res) => {
    res.json({ message: \`Fetched article \${req.params.id}\` });
  })
  .put((req, res) => {
    res.json({ message: \`Updated article \${req.params.id}\` });
  })
  .delete((req, res) => {
    res.status(204).send(); // 204 No Content
  });

export default router;`}},{type:"mistakes",heading:{en:"6. Common Routing Mistakes",hi:"6. Routing Mein Hone Wali Common Galtiyan"},mistakes:[{mistake:{en:"Placing a parameterized route before a static route (`/users/:id` before `/users/profile`).",hi:"Specific route se pehle parameterized route likh dena (`/users/:id` pehle aur `/users/profile` baad mein)."},correction:{en:"Express evaluates routes in sequential order. `/users/:id` captures the string 'profile' as the `:id` parameter, completely blocking `/users/profile` from ever running. Always place static routes first.",hi:"Hamesha specific static routes ko dynamic routes ke upar likhein taaki Express pehle exact match dhoonde."},code:`// BUG: /users/profile will NEVER trigger!
router.get('/users/:id', (req, res) => res.send('User ID: ' + req.params.id));
router.get('/users/profile', (req, res) => res.send('User Profile')); // Shadowed!

// FIX: Reverse the order!
router.get('/users/profile', (req, res) => res.send('User Profile'));
router.get('/users/:id', (req, res) => res.send('User ID: ' + req.params.id));`},{mistake:{en:"Treating req.params and req.query as numbers directly without parsing.",hi:"`req.params` aur `req.query` ko direct number samajh lena."},correction:{en:"Values from URL paths and query strings are ALWAYS strings. Always cast them using `Number()`, `parseInt()`, or `parseFloat()` before mathematical or strict equality comparisons.",hi:"URL se aane wali har value string hoti hai. Numbers ke saath compare karne ke liye `parseInt(req.params.id, 10)` use karein."},code:`// BUG:
if (req.params.id === 5) {} // ALWAYS false! ("5" === 5 is false)

// FIX:
if (parseInt(req.params.id, 10) === 5) {} // Works!`}]},{type:"summary",heading:{en:"7. Production Routing Best Practices",hi:"7. Production Routing Ke Best Practices"},body:{en:"- **Keep Route Files Declarative**: Route files should only define paths and link to controller functions (`router.get('/:id', userController.getUserById)`). Keep heavy business logic out of route files.\n- **RESTful Naming Conventions**: Use plural nouns for resources (`/api/products`, not `/api/getProducts`). Use HTTP verbs (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE) to denote actions rather than baking verbs into URLs.\n- **Use Regex Validations on Params**: Protect parameterized routes from garbage inputs: `router.get('/users/:id(\\\\d+)', ...)` only matches numeric user IDs!",hi:"- **Route Files Ko Clean Rakhein**: Route files mein sirf URL mapping honi chahiye, business logic controllers mein honi chahiye.\n- **RESTful Naming Conventions**: Hamesha plural nouns use karein (`/api/users`, na ki `/api/getUsers`).\n- **Regex Param Validation**: Agar ID sirf number ho sakti hai toh `/users/:id(\\\\d+)` likhein taaki invalid string aane par automatic 404 ho jaye."}},{type:"interview",heading:{en:"8. Top Interview Questions & Answers",hi:"8. Top Interview Sawal Aur Jawab"},questions:[{q:{en:"What is the difference between `req.params` and `req.query` in Express?",hi:"Express mein `req.params` aur `req.query` mein kya antar hota hai?"},a:{en:"req.params contains route parameters defined directly within the route path pattern (e.g. `/users/:id` -> `req.params.id`), used to identify a specific entity. req.query contains optional query string parameters appended after the `?` in the URL (e.g. `/users?role=admin&page=2` -> `req.query.role`), used for filtering, searching, and pagination.",hi:"req.params route path ke andar ke dynamic variables hote hain (jaise `/users/:id`), jo kisi specific record ko pehchanne ke kaam aate hain. req.query URL ke aage `?` laga kar bheje gaye optional key-value pairs hote hain (jaise `?role=admin&page=2`), jo data ko filter, sort ya paginate karne ke kaam aate hain."}},{q:{en:"What happens if a route definition `/users/:id` is placed before `/users/settings`?",hi:"Agar `/users/:id` route ko `/users/settings` se pehle likh diya jaye toh kya hoga?"},a:{en:"Because Express evaluates routes sequentially, any incoming request for `/users/settings` will be captured by the `/users/:id` route handler, where `req.params.id` will equal the string 'settings'. The `/users/settings` handler will never be executed. Specific routes must always precede generic parameterized routes.",hi:"Express routes ko sequence mein check karta hai. `/users/settings` par aane wali request ko `/users/:id` pakad lega aur `req.params.id` ki value 'settings' ban jayegi. Is wajah se `/users/settings` wala handler kabhi chal hi nahi payega."}},{q:{en:"What is the purpose of `express.Router()`?",hi:"`express.Router()` ka main purpose kya hota hai?"},a:{en:"express.Router() creates an isolated instance of middleware and routes. It acts like a mini-application, allowing developers to split a monolithic application into modular, maintainable route files grouped by feature or resource (e.g. authRoutes, productRoutes, orderRoutes) and mount them cleanly on the main app.",hi:"express.Router() ek isolated mini-application banata hai jisse hum poore app ke routes ko alag-alag feature files (jaise userRoutes, productRoutes) mein tod kar organize kar sakte hain aur main app par mount kar sakte hain."}}]},{type:"summary",heading:{en:"9. Summary Cheatsheet",hi:"9. Summary Cheatsheet"},body:{en:"- **Router**: `const router = express.Router()`.\n- **req.params**: Extracted from `/path/:param`.\n- **req.query**: Extracted from `/path?key=value`.\n- **Data Type**: Params & Queries are ALWAYS strings.\n- **Rule**: Place static routes before dynamic parameterized routes.",hi:"- **Router**: `express.Router()` modular files ke liye.\n- **req.params**: Dynamic path variables (:id).\n- **req.query**: Query strings (?search=test).\n- **String Rule**: Hamesha `Number()` se cast karein.\n- **Order Rule**: Static routes pehle, dynamic routes baad mein."}}],quiz:[{q:{en:"Given the URL `http://localhost:5000/api/users/42?status=active`, which expression accesses the string '42'?",hi:"URL `http://localhost:5000/api/users/42?status=active` mein '42' access karne ke liye kya use karenge?"},options:[{en:"req.params.id (if route is /api/users/:id)",hi:"req.params.id (agar route /api/users/:id ho)"},{en:"req.query.id",hi:"req.query.id"},{en:"req.body.id",hi:"req.body.id"},{en:"req.url[42]",hi:"req.url[42]"}],answerIndex:0,explanation:{en:"Path segments matched by a colon (e.g. :id) are stored on the req.params object.",hi:"Colon (:id) se match hone wale URL path variables req.params par milte hain."}},{q:{en:"What data type is `req.query.page` when a client requests `/items?page=3`?",hi:"Jab client `/items?page=3` request karta hai toh `req.query.page` ka data type kya hota hai?"},options:[{en:'string ("3")',hi:'string ("3")'},{en:"number (3)",hi:"number (3)"},{en:"boolean (true)",hi:"boolean (true)"},{en:"undefined",hi:"undefined"}],answerIndex:0,explanation:{en:"All query string values are parsed as strings by default in Express.",hi:"Express mein query parameters hamesha string ke roop mein aate hain."}},{q:{en:"Why should `router.get('/products/deals', ...)` be defined BEFORE `router.get('/products/:id', ...)`?",hi:"`router.get('/products/deals')` ko `router.get('/products/:id')` se pehle kyun define karna chahiye?"},options:[{en:"Otherwise, Express will match 'deals' as the `:id` parameter and shadow the deals route",hi:"Warna Express 'deals' ko `:id` parameter samajh lega aur deals wala route block ho jayega"},{en:"Express throws a syntax error if dynamic routes come second",hi:"Dynamic route baad mein aane par Express syntax error deta hai"},{en:"To optimize database connection pools",hi:"Database speed badhane ke liye"},{en:"It makes no difference in Express",hi:"Express mein isse koi farak nahi padta"}],answerIndex:0,explanation:{en:"Express routes match in sequential order. A generic parameter route catches all subsequent matching paths unless static routes are mounted first.",hi:"Express upar se neeche match karta hai. Dynamic :id route static routes ko shadow kar deta hai agar wo pehle define ho."}},{question:{en:"What is the core architectural purpose of Routing, Route Parameters & Query Strings in the modern full-stack MERN ecosystem?",hi:"Modern full-stack MERN ecosystem mein Routing, Route Params (:id) & Query Strings (?search=) ka mukhya architectural maksad kya hota hai?"},options:[{en:"It manages physical computer cooling and power supply",hi:"Ye physical computer cooling aur power supply manage karta hai"},{en:"It provides structured, robust, and scalable patterns for handling routing, route parameters & query strings with high performance and maintainability",hi:"Ye high performance aur maintainability ke saath Routing, Route Params (:id) & Query Strings (?search=) ko handle karne ka structured aur scalable pattern provide karta hai"},{en:"It completely replaces JavaScript with binary machine code in browser tabs",hi:"Ye browser tabs mein JavaScript ko binary machine code se replace karta hai"},{en:"It is only used for printing documents to physical printers",hi:"Ye sirf physical printers par documents print karne ke liye hai"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Routing, Route Parameters & Query Strings establishes clean separation of concerns, ensuring predictable data flow, robust error handling, and optimal runtime performance in production.",hi:"Routing, Route Params (:id) & Query Strings (?search=) clean architecture aur separation of concerns deta hai jisse application scalable aur maintainable banti hai."}},{question:{en:"What critical development bottleneck or anti-pattern does Routing, Route Parameters & Query Strings directly resolve?",hi:"Routing, Route Params (:id) & Query Strings (?search=) kis critical development bottleneck ya anti-pattern ko seedhe solve karta hai?"},options:[{en:"It replaces chaotic, tightly coupled ad-hoc logic with declarative, predictable control flow and structured data contracts",hi:"Ye chaotic aur tightly coupled logic ko hata kar declarative, predictable flow aur structured data contracts deta hai"},{en:"It forces the operating system to shut down when errors occur",hi:"Error aane par ye operating system band kar deta hai"},{en:"It deletes all database records older than 24 hours automatically",hi:"Ye 24 ghante purane DB records delete karta hai"},{en:"It blocks all outgoing HTTP network requests to conserve bandwidth",hi:"Ye bandwidth bachane ke liye network requests block karta hai"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Without Routing, Route Parameters & Query Strings, applications suffer from brittle code, maintenance overhead, and unhandled edge cases that manifest as production crashes.",hi:"Routing, Route Params (:id) & Query Strings (?search=) ke bina code brittle ho jata hai aur production mein unexpected errors aate hain."}},{question:{en:"When reasoning about Routing, Route Parameters & Query Strings, how is its mental model best conceptualized through real-world analogies?",hi:"Routing, Route Params (:id) & Query Strings (?search=) ko real-world analogies ke zariye kaise best samjha ja sakta hai?"},options:[{en:"As a completely offline computer with zero network or database connections",hi:"Ek offline computer ki tarah jisme koi connection na ho"},{en:"As a disciplined, coordinated workflow where inputs are validated and processed through standardized checkpoints rather than ad-hoc handling",hi:"Ek disciplined workflow ki tarah jahan data ko structured checkpoints ke zariye step-by-step process kiya jata hai"},{en:"As a random number generator with non-deterministic output",hi:"Random number generator ki tarah jiska koi niyam na ho"},{en:"As a static text document that cannot be modified or read",hi:"Static text document jo padha na ja sake"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Real-world workflow analogies help engineers visualize component boundaries, request lifecycles, and data transformations intuitively.",hi:"Real-world analogies component boundaries aur request lifecycle ko visual aur intuitive banati hain."}},{question:{en:"When declaring and implementing Routing, Route Parameters & Query Strings, what syntactic convention is essential to prevent runtime errors?",hi:"Routing, Route Params (:id) & Query Strings (?search=) ko declare aur implement karte waqt kaunsa syntax niyam runtime errors rokne ke liye zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"Adhering strictly to required parameters, handling asynchronous promises/callbacks cleanly, and verifying return value types",hi:"Zaroori parameters sahi pass karna, async promises ko handle karna aur return value types verify karna"},{en:"Wrapping every line of code inside an eval() execution block",hi:"Har line ko eval() block mein wrap karna"},{en:"Omitting import and require statements to reduce file size",hi:"File size ghatane ke liye import statements hatana"},{en:"Writing all code on a single continuous line without whitespace",hi:"Bina whitespace ke single line par code likhna"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Following standard ES6+ syntax contracts and properly handling promise resolution ensures execution safety and eliminates TypeError exceptions.",hi:"ES6+ syntax aur promise handling ke standard rules follow karne se TypeError aur crashes nahi aate."}},{question:{en:"What is a common pitfall developers encounter when working with Routing, Route Parameters & Query Strings?",hi:"Routing, Route Params (:id) & Query Strings (?search=) ke saath kaam karte waqt developers aksar kaunsi aam galati karte hain?"},options:[{en:"Writing unit tests before implementing features",hi:"Feature likhne se pehle unit tests likhna"},{en:"Failing to handle failure edge cases, mutating shared state directly, or neglecting defensive validation guard clauses",hi:"Failure edge cases ko handle na karna, shared state direct mutate karna ya validation guard clauses na lagana"},{en:"Using strict equality checks (===) instead of loose equality (==)",hi:"Loose equality ke badle strict equality use karna"},{en:"Writing clear inline code documentation",hi:"Clear inline code comments likhna"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Neglecting edge cases and error handling causes silent regressions and race conditions that surface under concurrent user workloads.",hi:"Edge cases aur error handling miss karne se high-traffic production load mein silent bugs paida hote hain."}},{question:{en:"According to production best practices, how should Routing, Route Parameters & Query Strings be architected for enterprise-grade stability?",hi:"Production best practices ke mutabiq enterprise-grade stability ke liye Routing, Route Params (:id) & Query Strings (?search=) ko kaise architect karna chahiye?"},options:[{en:"Enforce modular boundaries, validate all incoming payloads against schemas, log structured context, and maintain pure functions where possible",hi:"Modular boundaries enforce karein, payloads ko schema se validate karein, structured logs rakhein aur pure functions use karein"},{en:"Hardcode sensitive database connection strings directly in client-side files",hi:"Database passwords ko client files mein hardcode karna"},{en:"Disable all linter rules and type warnings globally",hi:"Linter aur type warnings ko globally disable karna"},{en:"Store all user session variables in global un-scoped memory arrays",hi:"Global memory arrays mein sessions store karna"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Enterprise-grade code prioritizes modularity, strict input validation, structured observability, and stateless designs.",hi:"Production hardening ke liye modular code, schema validation aur observability standard rules hote hain."}},{question:{en:"How does proper optimization of Routing, Route Parameters & Query Strings impact application memory and CPU consumption?",hi:"Routing, Route Params (:id) & Query Strings (?search=) ko sahi dhang se optimize karne par application memory aur CPU par kya asar padta hai?"},options:[{en:"It increases server CPU temperature to 100 degrees Celsius",hi:"Server CPU temperature 100 degrees kar deta hai"},{en:"It minimizes redundant computations, eliminates memory leaks from uncleaned references, and maintains low latency under high concurrency",hi:"Ye redundant computations ghatata hai, memory leaks khatam karta hai aur high concurrency mein low latency maintain karta hai"},{en:"It doubles heap RAM allocation unconditionally",hi:"Heap RAM ko zabardasti double karta hai"},{en:"Optimization has zero measurable impact in modern web engines",hi:"Modern web engines par optimization ka koi asar nahi hota"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Preventing unnecessary allocations and cleaning up resources ensures low garbage collection pressure and predictable response times.",hi:"Memory leak rokne aur unnecessary allocations hatane se Garbage Collector par load kam rehta hai aur response fast rehta hai."}},{question:{en:"What security principle is non-negotiable when handling data within Routing, Route Parameters & Query Strings?",hi:"Routing, Route Params (:id) & Query Strings (?search=) mein data handle karte waqt kaunsa security principle non-negotiable hota hai?"},options:[{en:"Never trust client-supplied input: always sanitize, authenticate, authorize, and validate against strict schemas on the server",hi:"Client data par blind trust na karein: server par hamesha sanitize, authenticate, authorize aur validate karein"},{en:"Trust all requests coming from mobile devices or web browsers blindly",hi:"Mobile ya browser se aane wali requests par blind trust karein"},{en:"Disable HTTPS and SSL certificates to maximize raw network throughput",hi:"Network throughput ke liye HTTPS band karein"},{en:"Expose database admin credentials to all registered users",hi:"Database admin credentials sabhi users ko expose karein"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Zero-Trust security dictates that every incoming request and data mutation must be validated and authenticated server-side before processing.",hi:"Zero-Trust security ke mutabiq har incoming mutation ko server par strictly validate aur authenticate kiya jana chahiye."}},{question:{en:"How does asynchronous non-blocking execution operate in Routing, Route Parameters & Query Strings?",hi:"Routing, Route Params (:id) & Query Strings (?search=) mein asynchronous non-blocking execution kaise kaam karta hai?"},options:[{en:"It freezes the entire operating system until each operation completes",hi:"Har operation complete hone tak operating system freeze rehta hai"},{en:"I/O operations return Promises or accept callbacks, delegating work to background threads/queues while the main thread remains free to handle incoming tasks",hi:"I/O operations Promises return karte hain aur background queues use karke main thread ko baaki requests ke liye free rakhte hain"},{en:"Async operations execute in reverse alphabetical order automatically",hi:"Async operations reverse alphabetical order mein chalte hain"},{en:"Async code only executes when triggered manually by a user click",hi:"Sirf manual user click par async code chalta hai"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Non-blocking asynchronous operations resolve via microtasks or event loop queues, ensuring the runtime thread serves concurrent requests smoothly.",hi:"Non-blocking model main thread ko free rakhta hai taaki server bina rukaawat ke multiple users ko simultaneously serve kar sake."}},{question:{en:"What is the recommended pattern for propagating errors that occur in Routing, Route Parameters & Query Strings?",hi:"Routing, Route Params (:id) & Query Strings (?search=) mein error aane par unhe propagate karne ka recommended pattern kya hai?"},options:[{en:"Intercepting the error, enriching it with operational context, and delegating to a centralized error handler or error boundary",hi:"Error ko intercept karna, debug context add karna, aur centralized error handler ya error boundary ko pass karna"},{en:"Swallowing errors silently with empty catch {} blocks to hide problems from logs",hi:"Khaali catch {} blocks se errors ko silently daba dena taaki logs mein na dikhein"},{en:"Shutting down the server machine power immediately",hi:"Server machine power turant band kar dena"},{en:"Sending internal raw stack traces and database credentials to end-user browsers",hi:"Raw stack trace aur DB passwords browser par bhej dena"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Centralized error propagation provides complete operational observability while shielding internal infrastructure details from end users.",hi:"Centralized error handling se system mein transparency rehti hai aur user ko clean, safe error messages milte hain."}},{question:{en:"When authoring unit or integration tests for Routing, Route Parameters & Query Strings, what must the test suite assert?",hi:"Routing, Route Params (:id) & Query Strings (?search=) ke liye automated tests likhte waqt test suite ko kya assert karna zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"Only that the JavaScript file can be saved to disk",hi:"Sirf ye ki file disk par save ho sake"},{en:"Both the happy path (expected inputs producing valid outputs) AND boundary edge cases (null, empty arrays, network timeouts, invalid types)",hi:"Happy path (valid data) AUR boundary edge cases (null, empty array, network timeout, invalid types) dono ko verify karna"},{en:"That the test suite takes at least 24 hours to finish running",hi:"Test suite ko 24 ghante chalna chahiye"},{en:"Testing is considered unnecessary in modern full-stack development",hi:"Modern development mein testing zaroori nahi hai"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Robust automated test suites verify both standard valid scenarios and defensive failure modes to prevent regressions during deployments.",hi:"Achhi testing valid inputs aur failure states dono ko assert karti hai taaki production deployments safe rahein."}},{question:{en:"How does modular design enhance code maintainability in Routing, Route Parameters & Query Strings?",hi:"Modular design Routing, Route Params (:id) & Query Strings (?search=) mein code maintainability ko kaise badhata hai?"},options:[{en:"By isolating distinct responsibilities into small, reusable, and independently testable units following the Single Responsibility Principle",hi:"Single Responsibility Principle ke zariye alag-alag kaamo ko chote, reusable aur testable units mein baant kar"},{en:"By combining all frontend, backend, and database code into a single 50,000-line script",hi:"Saara code ek hi 50,000-line script mein daal kar"},{en:"By removing all function names and replacing them with random numbers",hi:"Function names hata kar random numbers likhna"},{en:"By forbidding code comments and documentation across the repository",hi:"Comments aur documentation ban kar dena"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Modularity reduces cognitive load, simplifies debugging, prevents ripple effects during changes, and enables seamless team collaboration.",hi:"Modular code se readability badhti hai, debugging aasan hoti hai aur ek jagah badlav karne par doosri jagah bugs nahi aate."}},{question:{en:"When application traffic scales 100x, how should Routing, Route Parameters & Query Strings be architected to support horizontal scaling?",hi:"Traffic 100x badhne par Routing, Route Params (:id) & Query Strings (?search=) ko horizontally scale karne ke liye kya design approach honi chahiye?"},options:[{en:"Ensure the component/service is completely stateless, offload shared session/state to Redis/MongoDB, and distribute traffic via a load balancer",hi:"Service ko completely stateless banayein, shared state ko Redis/DB par shift karein aur load balancer se traffic distribute karein"},{en:"Store all user session variables in local in-memory JavaScript objects on the web server",hi:"Server ki local RAM mein session variables store karna"},{en:"Reboot the production server manually whenever memory usage exceeds 10%",hi:"Memory 10% cross hote hi server manually reboot karna"},{en:"Block 95% of incoming users using firewall rules",hi:"95% users ko firewall se block kar dena"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Stateless service architecture guarantees that any container instance can handle any incoming request, enabling dynamic auto-scaling without session loss.",hi:"Stateless architecture auto-scaling ka base hai jahan naye containers bina session loss ke instant traffic handle kar sakte hain."}},{question:{en:"In the full-stack MERN paradigm, where does Routing, Route Parameters & Query Strings properly belong and execute?",hi:"Full-stack MERN architecture mein Routing, Route Params (:id) & Query Strings (?search=) kahan belong karta hai aur kahan execute hota hai?"},options:[{en:"In its designated architectural tier (Client browser UI, Express API backend, or MongoDB database) with clean API contracts connecting them",hi:"Apne designated tier (Browser UI, Express API backend, ya MongoDB) mein clean API contracts ke saath"},{en:"Directly on the end-user's local router firmware",hi:"User ke local router firmware par"},{en:"Inside the computer motherboard BIOS chip",hi:"Motherboard BIOS chip mein"},{en:"All MERN code runs strictly inside the MongoDB database engine",hi:"Saara MERN code sirf MongoDB ke andar chalta hai"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Maintaining clear structural boundaries between client rendering, backend orchestration, and database persistence is the defining trait of MERN.",hi:"Client UI, backend server aur database ke beech saaf boundary maintain karna MERN architecture ka mukhya niyam hai."}},{question:{en:"What telemetry metric or observability signal is most crucial for diagnosing issues with Routing, Route Parameters & Query Strings in production?",hi:"Production mein Routing, Route Params (:id) & Query Strings (?search=) ki problems diagnose karne ke liye sabse zaroori telemetry metric kaunsi hoti hai?"},options:[{en:"The desktop monitor brightness setting of the client",hi:"Client ke monitor ki brightness"},{en:"Latency percentiles (p95/p99), error rates (HTTP 4xx/5xx), throughput (RPS), and heap memory allocation deltas",hi:"Latency percentiles (p95/p99), error rates (4xx/5xx), throughput (RPS), aur heap memory allocation deltas"},{en:"The number of files in the project's root folder",hi:"Root folder mein files ki sankhya"},{en:"The physical keyboard model used by the engineer",hi:"Engineer ke keyboard ka model"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Observability platforms monitor p95/p99 latencies, error frequencies, and memory utilization to identify bottlenecks and regressions early.",hi:"p95/p99 latencies aur error rates monitor karne se crashes aane se pehle hi bottlenecks pakad mein aa jaate hain."}},{question:{en:"Why is eliminating unintended side effects essential when authoring logic for Routing, Route Parameters & Query Strings?",hi:"Routing, Route Params (:id) & Query Strings (?search=) ka logic likhte waqt unintended side effects ko khatam karna kyun zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"Side effects introduce unpredictability, corrupt shared state, cause race conditions, and make concurrent code nearly impossible to debug",hi:"Side effects se code unpredictable banta hai, shared state corrupt hoti hai aur race conditions create hoti hain"},{en:"Side effects permanently erase the developer's Git commit history",hi:"Git history permanently delete ho jaati hai"},{en:"Side effects are strictly required by the JavaScript ECMAScript standard",hi:"ECMAScript mein side effects required hain"},{en:"Side effects make all algorithms execute in O(1) time",hi:"Saare algorithms O(1) time mein chalte hain"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Pure and predictable logic produces the same output for identical inputs, guaranteeing thread safety, easy caching, and high reliability.",hi:"Pure logic se shared state safe rehti hai aur same input par hamesha consistent aur predictable output milta hai."}},{question:{en:"How should client-side state be kept in sync with backend server mutations in Routing, Route Parameters & Query Strings?",hi:"Routing, Route Params (:id) & Query Strings (?search=) mein client-side state aur backend server data ko sync mein kaise rakha jata hai?"},options:[{en:"By forcing a complete hard page refresh every 3 seconds",hi:"Har 3 second mein poora page hard refresh karke"},{en:"Using optimistic UI updates with error rollback, automated query cache invalidation (TanStack Query/RTK), or WebSocket change streams",hi:"Optimistic UI updates with rollback, automated query cache invalidation ya WebSocket push streams use karke"},{en:"By disabling all database update operations permanently",hi:"Database updates ko permanently band karke"},{en:"By saving user state in local CSV files on the server desktop",hi:"Server desktop par CSV files save karke"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Modern full-stack architectures synchronize state seamlessly using query cache invalidation, optimistic updates, and real-time socket events.",hi:"Modern apps cache invalidation aur optimistic UI use karti hain taaki UI bina screen reload ke instantly updated rahe."}},{question:{en:"Why is thorough resource cleanup (clearing timers, closing sockets, aborting in-flight requests) critical in Routing, Route Parameters & Query Strings?",hi:"Routing, Route Params (:id) & Query Strings (?search=) mein resource cleanup (timers clear karna, sockets band karna, network abort karna) kyun zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"To prevent memory leaks where unreachable or orphaned objects remain retained in heap memory, causing gradual performance degradation and crashes",hi:"Memory leaks rokne ke liye taaki unneeded objects RAM mein jama na hon aur server crash na ho"},{en:"To delete the client's local disk partition",hi:"Client ka local disk partition delete karne ke liye"},{en:"Because JavaScript engines allow only 5 variables in RAM",hi:"JS engine sirf 5 variables allow karta hai"},{en:"Cleanup is unnecessary because garbage collection handles 100% of event listeners automatically",hi:"Cleanup ki zaroorat nahi hoti"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Unclosed connections and dangling event listeners create references that prevent garbage collection, leading to severe memory leaks over time.",hi:"Dangling listeners aur unclosed connections memory leaks banate hain jo V8 heap ko exhaust karke process crash kar dete hain."}}]};export{e as default};
